WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.101
Guanyin recited the Tight Headband spell.

2
00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:11.621
Both Wukongs fell to the ground, howling in pain.

3
00:00:11.622 --> 00:00:15.078
"Please stop!" they cried.

4
00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:22.258
Guanyin stopped reciting the spell, and the two monkeys stood back up.

5
00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:24.442
The bodhisattva frowned.

6
00:00:24.443 --> 00:00:28.269
"I still don't know which of you is the real Wukong.

7
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.352
[g@You should both go to Heaven.

8
00:00:30.353 --> 00:00:33.392
The real Wukong used to live there.@g]

9
00:00:33.393 --> 00:00:37.500
Maybe the Jade Emperor can tell who is who."

10
00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.362
[g@"Good idea," said one Wukong.

11
00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:41.826
He pointed at the other.@g]

12
00:00:41.827 --> 00:00:46.529
"The Jade Emperor will see that this monkey is a fake!"

13
00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:52.328
"I'm not a fake!" cried the other monkey. "You are!"

14
00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:54.878
He tried to strike the other Wukong.

15
00:00:54.879 --> 00:00:59.325
But that one dodged the blow and swung back.

16
00:00:59.326 --> 00:01:06.883
The two monkeys were still fighting when they arrived at the southern gate of Heaven.

17
00:01:06.884 --> 00:01:09.191
[g@The guard narrowed his eyes.

18
00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:11.885
"Wukong? Is that you?"@g]

19
00:01:11.886 --> 00:01:15.934
"Yes, it's me," said both of the Wukongs.

20
00:01:15.935 --> 00:01:19.647
"I must speak with the Jade Emperor," said one monkey.

21
00:01:19.648 --> 00:01:21.478
[g@He pointed at the other monkey.

22
00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:24.281
"He's a fake Wukong!"@g]

23
00:01:24.282 --> 00:01:27.683
"I'm not a fake Wukong!" said the other monkey.

24
00:01:27.684 --> 00:01:29.276
[g@"I'm the real one!

25
00:01:29.277 --> 00:01:33.638
I must speak with the Jade Emperor!"@g]

26
00:01:33.639 --> 00:01:38.867
The guard allowed both Wukongs to enter Heaven.

27
00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:41.772
[i@Crash! Clang! Bang!@i]

28
00:01:41.773 --> 00:01:48.510
Spirits and gods fled as the two Wukongs fought all over Heaven.

29
00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:54.259
The monkeys knocked over statues and trees.

30
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.224
Still fighting, they stormed into the Cloud Palace.

31
00:01:59.225 --> 00:02:03.358
When the Jade Emperor saw them, he was furious.

32
00:02:03.359 --> 00:02:06.923
"What's going on?" he boomed.

33
00:02:06.924 --> 00:02:10.396
"Your Majesty!" said one of the Wukongs.

34
00:02:10.397 --> 00:02:12.059
[g@"Please punish this monkey.

35
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.367
He's pretending to be me."@g]

36
00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:16.973
[g@"Punish [i@him!@i]" cried the other.

37
00:02:16.974 --> 00:02:20.402
"He's pretending to be me!"@g]

38
00:02:20.403 --> 00:02:24.416
"Stand still, both of you," said the Jade Emperor.

39
00:02:24.417 --> 00:02:30.725
"Let me get a good look at you."

40
00:02:30.726 --> 00:02:36.634
The two Wukongs stood still as the Jade Emperor looked carefully at them.

41
00:02:36.635 --> 00:02:38.810
Finally the emperor shrugged.

42
00:02:38.811 --> 00:02:40.528
[g@"You look exactly alike.

43
00:02:40.529 --> 00:02:43.453
I can't tell who is who."@g]

44
00:02:43.454 --> 00:02:47.622
One of the Wukongs swung at the other with his iron bar.

45
00:02:47.623 --> 00:02:49.916
"I'm the real Wukong!"

46
00:02:49.917 --> 00:02:53.731
"No!" The other Wukong blocked the bar and swung back.

47
00:02:53.732 --> 00:02:58.379
"I'm the real Wukong!"

48
00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.690
"Both of you, leave at once!" thundered the Jade Emperor.

49
00:03:02.691 --> 00:03:05.612
[g@"One Wukong is bad enough.

50
00:03:05.613 --> 00:03:07.897
I don't want two of you around.@g]

51
00:03:07.898 --> 00:03:15.045
You can fight somewhere else!"

52
00:03:15.046 --> 00:03:18.977
The two monkeys kept fighting as they headed out of the palace.

53
00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:23.009
The spirit of the planet Venus followed them.

54
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.917
"Wukong, wait," said the spirit.

55
00:03:25.918 --> 00:03:28.673
Both monkeys stopped to look at him.

56
00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:32.263
"Go to the Land of Darkness," said Venus.

57
00:03:32.264 --> 00:03:38.855
"Maybe the Judge of the Dead can tell you apart."

58
00:03:38.856 --> 00:03:43.802
Soon the two Wukongs were standing before the Judge of the Dead.

59
00:03:43.803 --> 00:03:45.584
[g@The judge shook his head.

60
00:03:45.585 --> 00:03:48.819
"You look exactly alike."@g]

61
00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.387
"Check the Directory," said one of the Wukongs.

62
00:03:52.388 --> 00:03:56.263
"Maybe it will have some information about a fake Sun Wukong."

63
00:03:56.264 --> 00:04:01.749
"Yes," said the other Wukong. "Check the Directory."

64
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:05.405
The judge nodded and opened the Directory.

65
00:04:05.406 --> 00:04:09.688
He turned the pages of the giant book, reading carefully.

66
00:04:09.689 --> 00:04:12.301
Finally he closed it.

67
00:04:12.302 --> 00:04:17.415
"There's no 'Fake Sun Wukong' in the Directory," said the judge.

68
00:04:17.416 --> 00:04:24.512
"I'm sorry. But I have no idea which one of you is the real Wukong."

69
00:04:24.513 --> 00:04:28.029
A spirit was sitting at a nearby desk.

70
00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:33.501
"I believe my pet beast, Curious Ear, can help," said the spirit.

71
00:04:33.502 --> 00:04:38.701
He took a step back, and a small beast crept out from under the desk.

72
00:04:38.702 --> 00:04:48.748
"Curious Ear can tell the true from the false," said the spirit.

73
00:04:48.749 --> 00:04:52.146
The beast stared hard at the two Wukongs.

74
00:04:52.147 --> 00:04:53.845
[g@Finally it spoke.

75
00:04:53.846 --> 00:05:01.118
"I know who the fake Sun Wukong is."@g]

